# Python Clean Code Standards

## Code Quality

- Remove all print statements except for error logging
- Resolve all flake8, pylint, mypy, and black warnings/errors
- Remove unused imports and variables
- Use meaningful variable and function names following snake_case convention

## Python-Specific Formatting

- Follow PEP 8 style guidelines
- Use black formatter for consistent formatting
- Maximum line length of 88 characters (black default)
- Use double quotes for strings consistently
- Remove trailing whitespace

## Python Best Practices

- Add type hints for all function parameters and return types
- Use f-strings for string formatting instead of .format() or %
- Prefer list/dict comprehensions over loops when readable
- Use pathlib.Path instead of os.path for file operations
- Follow user rule: no comments except for really hard/complex code

## Error Handling & Logging

- Log only errors (following user rule)
- Use proper exception types and messages
- Handle exceptions with specific except clauses, avoid bare except:
- Use logging module instead of print for error messages

## Imports & Dependencies

- Group imports: standard library, third-party, local imports
- Use absolute imports when possible
- Remove unused imports (isort + autoflake)

## Final Python Checklist

- [ ] All linting errors resolved (flake8, pylint, mypy)
- [ ] Black formatting applied
- [ ] No unused imports or variables
- [ ] Type hints added where needed
- [ ] Error handling follows logging standards
- [ ] PEP 8 compliance verified
